## 1. Naming Conventions (C5)

| Kind | Convention | Example | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| {{kind}} | `{{convention}}` | `{{example}}` | {{note}} |

- Domain glossary terms are used verbatim; banned vague names: `data`, `info`, `tmp`, `val`, `Manager`, `Helper`, `Utils`, `process()`, `handle()`.

## 2. Size Thresholds & Decomposition (C6)

| Unit | Limit | Remedy when exceeded |
|---|---|---|
| Function / method | {{fn_limit}} | Extract cohesive private helper steps. |
| File / module | {{file_limit}} | Split by responsibility into dedicated modules ({{clean_architecture_link}}). |
| Parameters | {{param_limit}} | Group cohesive inputs into a typed model/object. |
| Nesting depth | {{nesting_limit}} | Use guard clauses and early returns. |

### Splitting Oversized Units
1. Identify distinct responsibilities that vary independently (input validation, domain rules, persistence, external I/O, presentation rendering).
2. Extract each piece with an intention-revealing name from §1 and place it per {{clean_architecture_link}}.
3. Update all call sites in the same task and delete the old code without leaving pass-through wrappers or compatibility aliases (**C1**).

## 3. Structure, Globals, Helper Locality, and Export Surface (C1, C15, C16, C17)

- **One concept, one place (C1)**: No pass-through wrappers or compatibility re-export shims.
- **No mutable module globals (C15)**: Module level holds only shared constants (`{{const_convention}}`), logger, and configuration settings.
- **Helper locality (C16)**: A helper used in one file stays private (`{{private_convention}}`) in that file; move only when imported by 2+ files into the owning domain module—never create `utils` or `helpers` buckets.
- **Explicit export surface (C17)**: Package entry/barrel files (`{{entry_file}}`) export only the symbols other modules actually import; no wildcard exports or leaked internals.

## 4. Static Types, Immutability, Constants & Comments (C7, C8, C9, C13)

- **Full static types (C9)**: `{{type_rules}}`
- **Immutable state & value objects (C13)**: `{{immutability_rules}}`
- **Named constants & enums (C7)**: `{{constants_rules}}`
- **Comments explain WHY (C8)**: Explain non-obvious constraints and trade-offs; never restate what the syntax already says.

